        <p class="define">Information hazards, or infohazards, are defined as 
            "A risk that arises from the dissemination or the potential
            dissemination of (true) information that may cause harm or enable some agent to cause
            harm." Accompanied with examples, this archive explores the typology of information hazards, and how, where, and why they manifest.
        </p>
